From: AlSukkar <dev@example.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] security: bump vulnerable libs across all projects + fix GenerateDepsFile race

This patch does two things:

1. Closes the NU1902/NU1903 vulnerability warnings that NuGet reports
   during restore across FOUR different csproj files (Tmds.DBus is a
   direct reference in three of them, not just the main project):

     Tmds.DBus 0.21.2                          GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9  (high)
     Tmds.DBus.Protocol 0.21.2                 GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9  (high)
     SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 2.1.11         GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q  (high)
     SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3.android 2.1.11  GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q  (high)
     System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 9.0.0    GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7  (moderate)
     System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 9.0.0    GHSA-846f-f764-76mx  (high)
     System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.0     GHSA-23rf-6693-g89p  (high)
     System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.0     (plus ~10 chained advisories)

   - GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj:
       * Tmds.DBus 0.21.2 -> 0.21.3 (direct ref)
       * Add explicit refs to SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_green 2.1.14,
         SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3.android 2.1.14,
         System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 9.0.21,
         System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.18
         (transitive deps pulled in via EF Core 10.0.3 /
          Microsoft.AspNet.WebApi.Client 6.0.0; NuGet picks the
          lowest satisfying version so explicit refs are required).
   - ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj:
       * Tmds.DBus 0.21.2 -> 0.21.3 (direct ref)
   - ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj:
       * Tmds.DBus 0.21.2 -> 0.21.3 (direct ref)
   - GalaxyBudsClient.Platform.Linux.csproj: NO CHANGE NEEDED.
     It already uses Tmds.DBus.Protocol 0.21.3 (patched); its
     vulnerability warnings come transitively through BlueZNet /
     MprisClient and will disappear once those two are bumped.

   All chosen versions are same-major.minor servicing patches;
   no API or behavior break.

2. Fixes the intermittent MSB4018 / GenerateDepsFile IOException
   that was failing the dotnet publish step:

       error MSB4018: The "GenerateDepsFile" task failed unexpectedly.
       System.IO.IOException: The process cannot access the file
         '.../GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.deps.json' because it is
         being used by another process.

   Root cause: the InstallAndroidDependencies step leaves behind
   orphan MSBuild worker nodes (and VBCSCompiler) that hold the
   deps.json file handle open. When the publish step then tries to
   rewrite that file, the OS denies access.

   Fix: set <GenerateDependencyFile>false</GenerateDependencyFile>
   on the Generators project. Source generators are loaded as
   analyzers; they never need deps.json at runtime, so not writing
   it eliminates the file-lock race entirely. (Defense in depth;
   also add `dotnet build-server shutdown` to the workflow between
   the two steps - see commit message footer.)

Verify after applying:
    dotnet nuget locals all --clear
    dotnet restore GalaxyBudsClient.Android/GalaxyBudsClient.Android.csproj
    # -> 0 NU1902/NU1903 warnings
    dotnet publish GalaxyBudsClient.Android/GalaxyBudsClient.Android.csproj \
      -c Release -f net10.0-android36.1 -p:NoDemo=true -o publish/
    # -> no MSB4018 / IOException

Recommended companion workflow change (NOT part of this patch since
the user already has their own yml - apply manually):

    - name: Install Android SDK dependencies
      run: |
        dotnet build "$CSPROJ" -t:InstallAndroidDependencies -f "$TFM" \
          -p:AndroidSdkDirectory="$ANDROID_SDK_DIR" \
          -p:AcceptAndroidSDKLicenses=True
        dotnet build-server shutdown   # <-- ADD THIS LINE

---
 .../GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.csproj           |  6 ++++++
 GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj          | 11 ++++++++++-
 ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj       |  2 +-
 ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.csproj b/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.csproj
index 31cacae..b338c7c 100644
--- a/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.csproj
+++ b/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators/GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.csproj
@@ -8,6 +8,12 @@
 
         <EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>true</EnforceExtendedAnalyzerRules>
         <IsRoslynComponent>true</IsRoslynComponent>
+
+        <!-- Source generators are loaded as analyzers and don't need a
+             runtime deps.json. Disabling it removes the file that orphan
+             MSBuild worker nodes were holding open across CI steps,
+             causing MSB4018 "GenerateDepsFile" IOException on publish. -->
+        <GenerateDependencyFile>false</GenerateDependencyFile>
     </PropertyGroup>
 
     <ItemGroup>
diff --git a/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj b/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj
index a4ee220..e53aa25 100644
--- a/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj
+++ b/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj
@@ -128,7 +128,16 @@
         <PackageReference Include="Serilog.Sinks.Trace" Version="4.0.0" />
         <!-- Workaround: force include SkiaSharp 3.x libraries for Linux; this is already implicitly the case for other platforms -->
         <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux" Version="3.119.1" />
-        <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.2" />
+        <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.3" />
+
+        <!-- Security overrides: force patched versions of transitive deps
+             pulled in via EF Core 10.0.3 / Microsoft.AspNet.WebApi.Client 6.0.0.
+             NuGet picks the lowest satisfying version, so explicit refs are
+             required to lift these above the vulnerable floor. -->
+        <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_green" Version="2.1.14" />
+        <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3.android" Version="2.1.14" />
+        <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="9.0.21" />
+        <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="9.0.18" />
     </ItemGroup>
 
 
